cord from the Adam controller but still fail/timeout overall, so the harness retries the stale teardown on the next test (`ZFSPersist`) and hits \"unknown device UUID\" because the device was already removed.\n\nThis exact `unknown device UUID` teardown-cascade signature (caused by an earlier SUSPECT/dead-device teardown failing non-atomically and poisoning the next test's cleanup) is a known, recurring issue — it appears in `live-ledger.md` for run #6 (2026-11-03), where it hit `TestKubeRegistrationLonghornDisks`, `TestAppLocalInfo`, `TestDevLocalInfo`, and `TestNetworkLocalChanges` with the identical error shape. It is not a new independent bug: it shares the same underlying SDN/broker outage root cause already recorded for `Shrink`, `Grow`, and `PersistTooFull` earlier in tonight's run, and the broader \"teardown doesn't surface partial success, so retries hit stale UUIDs\" pattern has been recurring since at least 2026-11-03.","time":{"start":1793834337000,"stop":1793834382500,"duration":45500}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"20e70146e2f4a00e.json","parameterValues":[]}